<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 92-day T-bill yields avg 3.962 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 92-day T-bill yields avg 3.962 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$3.2 billion of 92-day Government of Canada treasury bills due December 27 was 3.962 percent, up from 3.758 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.7 billion of 182-day T-bills due March 27, 1997 was 4.260 percent, down from 4.265 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 357-day T-bills due September 18, 1997 was 4.663 percent, down from 4.682 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$900 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.15 billion of C$6.9 billion bills due Oct. 3. </p>
